#tr.en: Ilšu-abūšu son of Sîn-nāṣir
5. i-gu-ru-szu-ma ih-li-qu2-szu 
#tr.ts: īgurūšūma iḫliqūšu
#tr.en: had rented it and (that) fled (from) him.
6. asz-szum _ansze_ bi-il-tim {disz}dingir-szu-a-bu-szu 
#tr.ts: aššum imērim biltim ilšu-abūšu
#tr.en: Because of the pack donkey, Ilšu-abūšu
7. {disz}ARAD-{d}en-lil2 u3 s,il2-li2-isz8-tar2 i-di-nu-ma 
#tr.ts: warad-enlil u ṣilli-ištar idīnūma
#tr.en: Warad-enlil and Ṣilli-ištar have started a lawsuit so
8. da-ia-nu i-na _ka2_ {d}utu 
#tr.ts: dayyānū ina bāb šamaš
#tr.en: the judges, at the Gate of Šamaš
9. i-na li-bi zimbir{ki} 
#tr.ts: ina li(b)bi sippar
#tr.en: in Sippar,
10. di-nam u2-sza-hi-zu-szu-nu-ti-ma 
#tr.ts: dīnam ušāḫizūšunūtīma
#tr.en: have granted them a trial and
11. a-na szu-ri-nim sza {d}utu 
#tr.ts: ana šuri(n)nim ša šamaš
#tr.en: (to take an oath) to the emblem of Šamaš,
12. da-ia-nu {disz}ARAD-{d}en-lil2 u3 s,il2-li2-isz8-tar2 
#tr.ts: dayyānū warad-enlil u ṣilli-ištar
#tr.en: the judges, Warad-enlil and Ṣilli-ištar
13. a-na dingir-szu-a-bu-szu id-di-nu-szu-<nu>-ma 
#tr.ts: ana ilšu-abūšu iddinūšunūma
